## 7. DISCONNECT HANDLING

### Keeper disconnects

| Feature                                               | Status | Notes                                                                 |
|-------------------------------------------------------|--------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Game continues without crash/lock                     | true   | No exceptions; remaining clients keep playing                         |
| Remaining clients set Keeper inactive / remove Keeper | true   | Despawned player removed from `_playerStates`                         |
| UI displays updated Keeper (new one)                  | true   | No explicit “X disconnected” banner, but Keeper id changes visibly    |
| Next validity check assigns new Keeper (hostless)     | true   | Fallback via `ElectKeeperFromLastResolvedRound` / `EnsureKeeperSelected` |

### Regular player disconnects

| Feature                                               | Status | Notes                                                                 |
|-------------------------------------------------------|--------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Game continues without crash/lock                     | true   |                                                                       |
| Remaining clients set player inactive / remove player | true   | Player disappears; no blocking references remain                      |

**Summary:**  
Disconnects (Keeper or regular) do not break the simulation or lockstep. Responsibility is handed to remaining players as intended.

